# Fledge Alpha — findings by Space Bunny

- Source: OpenCode Zen (`opencode/fledge-alpha-free`; litellm route `opencode/fledge-alpha`)
- Date: 2026-10-02 (UTC)
- Overview and scoring methodology: `../../model-comparison.md`
- Cross-model signed log: `../../model-findings.md`

> **SELF-EXCLUDED — no verified public benchmark numbers.** Every benchmark row
> below reads "no verified public score found". That is the finding, and it is why
> this file is saved as `.md.excluded` rather than a scored `.md`. Per the template's
> SELF-EXCLUSION rule, no placeholder scores were invented: one fabricated number
> would drag the mean for every reader. `pnpm sync` ignores `.md.excluded` files.

## Model card

- **Name:** Fledge Alpha (Zen listing: **Fledge Alpha Free**)
- **Short description:** A $0 OpenCode Zen free-tier model with no disclosed vendor. OpenCode curates and benchmarks model/provider *combinations* for its coding-agent catalogue, but publishes no per-model capability table for Fledge Alpha — its own data page leaves Context, Output and Knowledge as "Unknown" and its comparison view renders all six capability dimensions as "No data; neutral placeholder". The model is confirmed real and in production use (see below), but its identity and quality are not publicly characterised.
- **Provider / access:** OpenCode Zen only. Model ID `opencode/fledge-alpha-free`, present in OpenCode's official public model list at `https://opencode.ai/zen/v1/models`. Served through the OpenAI-compatible Zen endpoint; reached via OpenCode's built-in `opencode` provider. Single provider — no OpenRouter, Vercel AI Gateway or models.dev listing exists.
- **Release / knowledge:** Released **2026-10-01** (modelcompare.dev's canonical record, refreshed daily). Knowledge cutoff not published; no vendor has claimed the model.
- **IDs:** `opencode/fledge-alpha-free` (Zen, verified in OpenCode's model list). **Correction to this folder's `meta.json`:** the curated stub carries id `opencode/fledge-alpha` and `contextWindow: "128K total"` with `scaffolded: true`; the verified Zen ID is `fledge-alpha-free` and the verified served context is 1,048,576 tokens, not 128K. The meta stub is the orchestrator's to correct per `tasks/sync-data.md`, so it is left untouched here.
- **Context window:** **1,048,576 tokens (1.05M) total / 131,072 max output** (modelcompare.dev canonical record, corroborated by LLM Directory's OpenCode Zen provider table). No long-context *retrieval* result is published at any window length.
- **Modalities:** Text and image **in**, text **out**. Reasoning: supported. Tool calling: supported. Structured output / JSON mode: **not reported** by any source. Temperature control: supported. Proprietary — no open weights.
- **Pricing (as of 2026-10-02):** **$0.00 in / $0.00 out.** LLM Directory lists `opencode/fledge-alpha-free` at `$0/1M` in and out on OpenCode Zen, and OpenCode's own usage page confirms **$0.00 total spend and $0.00 average cost per session** across 116,485 completed sessions. OpenCode's Zen privacy section states that during a free period, collected data may be used to improve the model — treat prompts on this tier as trainable, and keep proprietary source and customer data off it.
- **Architecture:** **Proprietary and undisclosed.** No vendor, no parameter count, no MoE/dense layout, no license. Nothing in the public record identifies what weights Fledge Alpha runs — it is not documented as a stealth re-badge of any named upstream model, and no such claim is made here.
- **Observed production scale (OpenCode usage data, trailing 2 months):** 204B tokens (+100% growth), 3.9K unique users, 116,485 completed sessions, **92% input-token cache ratio**, ~1.7M average tokens per session, ranked **#20** by observed OpenCode token volume. Cache ratio and session size confirm heavy long-context agentic use in practice.
- **Reliability caveat (verified 2026-10-02):** the endpoint was failing broadly that day — OpenCode issue #52703 records `fledge-alpha-free` "almost always" emitting `Upstream request failed: Endpoint is unavailable` through 6+ retries until outright failure (closed as not planned; the reporter notes the same error class on other Zen free models, suggesting a gateway-wide free-tier problem). Issue #52691 separately records `fledge-alpha-free` returning `finish_reason: "tool_calls"` with an empty delta, breaking OpenAI-compatible tool-call parsing.

### Raw benchmarks found

Agent / tool use:

- No verified public benchmark numbers were found for Fledge Alpha. OpenCode's own capability view renders every dimension as "No data; neutral placeholder", including Tool use.
- Tool calling is *declared* supported, and the model is in real agentic use (92% cache ratio, 1.7M-token sessions), but declaration and usage volume are not measurements of tool-use quality.
- Terminal-Bench 2.1 / Tau3 / Tau2 / GDPval-AA / Claw-Eval / Toolathon / MCP-Atlas: no verified public score found

Reasoning / knowledge:

- No verified public benchmark numbers were found. OpenCode's data page lists Knowledge as "Unknown".
- Reasoning support is declared; no GPQA Diamond, HLE, LCR, CritPt, Artificial Analysis Index or Omniscience figure exists.
- Fledge Alpha is absent from the Artificial Analysis LLM Leaderboard (250+ models), Vals AI's index, llm-stats and BenchLM.

Coding:

- No verified public benchmark numbers were found. No SWE-bench Verified, SWE-Pro, Terminal-Bench, LiveCodeBench, SciCode or Vibe Code Bench entry exists for this model anywhere.
- **No other model's numbers are transferred to it.** OpenCode Zen's marketing claim that Zen models are "tested and benchmarked" is a statement about model/provider routing, not a published per-model capability score for Fledge Alpha.

Long context:

- No verified long-context retrieval result (no MRCR / RULER / GraphWalks figure at any window length). The 1,048,576-token served limit and the observed 92% cache ratio with ~1.7M-token sessions are capacity facts, not retrieval-quality evidence.

Sources consulted (all accessed 2026-10-02): OpenCode's official Zen model list `https://opencode.ai/zen/v1/models` (confirms `fledge-alpha-free` exists); OpenCode's Zen docs `https://opencode.ai/docs/zen` (privacy/data-use policy for free tiers); OpenCode usage page `https://opencode.ai/data/unknown/fledge-alpha` (204B tokens, 3.9K users, 116,485 sessions, 92% cache ratio, $0.00 spend, Context/Output/Knowledge "Unknown", all six normalized dimensions "No data; neutral placeholder"); OpenCode comparison view vs GPT-5 Nano (same hollow-points rendering); modelcompare.dev `opencode/fledge-alpha-free` (2026-10-01 release date, 1.05M context, 131K max output, text+image in / text out, reasoning + tool calling, structured output unreported, proprietary, single provider); LLM Directory's OpenCode Zen provider table (`$0/1M` in and out); OpenCode GitHub issues #52616, #52691 and #52703 (the "Endpoint is unavailable" and tool-call-delta failures of 2026-10-02). Negative confirmations: no Fledge entry on Artificial Analysis, Vals AI, llm-stats or BenchLM; no Brave/Bing/DuckDuckGo/Qwant/Mojeek/Ecosia/Startpage result reports any benchmark, score or vendor for this model.

### Normalized scores (1–100)

> Scores are intentionally omitted. The template's SELF-EXCLUSION rule applies: zero
> verified public benchmark numbers means every quality dimension would be an
> invention, and `pnpm sync` would read those inventions as evidence. Capability
> declarations, a 1.05M context window and a $0 price are real and documented above,
> but none of them measures tool use, reasoning or coding quality. Writing a scored
> `.md` here would convert "we could not measure it" into a quality claim.

